.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt FSCK_OXFS 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsck_oxfs
.Nd check and repair an oxfs file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fnpy
.Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks the oxfs file system on
.Ar device ,
a raw disk partition such as
.Pa /dev/gpt/rootfs ,
and repairs it.
The file system must not be mounted read-write: the kernel refuses to let its
raw device be written then.
.Pp
oxfs writes a file's data and size later than its names and its allocation
.Pq Xr update 8 ,
in an order that leaves the file system consistent after a crash except for a
few things:
blocks marked in use that no file holds, files with no name left, and link
counts off by a rename or removal that didn't finish.
.Nm
finds and repairs these in five phases:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
every inode's blocks are checked against the size of the file system and
against each other;
.It
the directory tree is walked from the root, checking every name;
.It
inodes with no name are found: a directory, or a file with links left, is
reconnected in
.Pa /lost+found
as
.Pa # Ns Ar inode
(a directory with everything under it), and a file with no links left (removed
while still open) is freed;
.It
link counts are compared with the names found;
.It
the block bitmap is rebuilt from the blocks the remaining files hold.
.El
Then the file system is marked clean.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f
Check the file system even if it is marked clean.
.It Fl n
Open the device read-only and report, repairing nothing.
This is also what happens with none of
.Fl n ,
.Fl p
and
.Fl y .
.It Fl p
Preen: skip a clean file system, repair what a crash leaves without asking,
and stop with exit status 8, having written nothing, at anything else.
.Xr rc 8
runs this at boot, through
.Xr fsck 8 .
.It Fl y
Repair everything: also clear inodes holding blocks that are out of range or
held twice, and remove names of free inodes.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the file system is clean or was repaired; 8 when it needs a manual
check
.Pq Fl p
or still has problems
.Pq Fl n .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /lost+found -compact
.It Pa /lost+found
Where files that lost their names are reconnected; made by the format, and by
.Nm
when it is missing and needed.
It grows to twelve blocks (180 names); past that, what can't be reconnected is
left as it is, and reported.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fsck 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr update 8
